WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:14.019
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday!

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:17.660
Hank, you were just greeted by people in Schaumburg, Illinois, where I've been visiting.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:22.820
Now I'm driving home, and I'm filming Brotherhood 2.0. while driving. Is that safe?

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:29.840
No! It's not safe! But if I don't film Brotherhood 2.0 while driving, when will I film it? I'm gonna get home right before midnight.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:35.910
Observation: people in passing cars look at you funny when you're driving down the road holding a camera in front of your face.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:36.840
Anyway, Hank,

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.909
I have to publicly state that I do not recommend video blogging while driving at 72 miles an hour.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.540
Unless you are nine months into a 12-month project and have not yet missed a day in that project.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.520
Okay Hank, I just pulled on merging traffic.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:53.780
Hank, I just passed an outlet mall, and I was like who goes to outlet malls anyway?

00:00:53.829 --> 00:00:58.468
And there was a billboard that said "At the outlet mall, come see the beef jerky outlet!"

00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:02.969
And I was like, "oh my god, must get over, must get in the right lane, must exit now!"

00:01:03.039 --> 00:01:07.018
But then there was this tragically long line of semi trucks, and I wasn't able to exit,

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:11.369
so I missed the beef jerky outlet! I mean Hank think of the beef jerky deals!

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.979
We should have more awesome outlets like that.

00:01:14.049 --> 00:01:17.849
Maybe we can go to Winner, South Dakota and build like a nerdfighter outlet mall.

00:01:17.849 --> 00:01:20.880
We could have like a "Put Stuff On Your Head" outlet that would sell like

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:26.400
85,000 different items that will fit on top of your head at wholesale prices. Of course, we'd have to have a Peeps outlet.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:31.320
They'd sell like every possible color of peeps, stamped into every shape and size in the world.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.130
By the way, Hank, my lifelong dream? A peep in the shape of me.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:40.229
And of course there would have to be a pants outlet, and as I envisioned it Hank all the pants we sell in our pants outlet would

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:46.499
be emblazoned with pineapples. The pineapple would tell you that you've got a pair of real legitimate 100% nerdfighter pants.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.279
Why a pineapple Hank? Because it's the international sign for welcome.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:55.460
It's like saying, "Welcome to my pants", and speaking of welcoming people to my pants Hank,

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:59.080
I'd like to thank you for getting the Brotherhood 2.0 forum "my pants" back up.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:00.780
Hank, I think I'm gonna go back to driving now.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:07.280
So that's it for me in Indiana, where the road is flat, the day is long and the corn is plentiful. I'll see you tomorrow.

00:02:08.369 --> 00:02:13.279
P.S. Hank it occurs to me that we've gone nine months in this video blog, and we've never really disagreed.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.729
So I've been thinking that maybe it's time for just a little tiny feud.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:21.860
I don't even know what we could disagree about, but maybe if we can come up with something then the nerdfighters can pick who wins?

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:27.740
All I know is this Hank: if we do have a feud, like a pirate at a ninja convention, you're gonna get pwned.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:35.929
P.P.S. Tomorrow's the yeti's birthday. Yay, Sarah! Oh, and Hank P.P.P.S., like it says on my friend Katie's arm, don't forget to be awesome.

